    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>On 30 December 1922 the Ukrainian SSR became one of the four founding republics of the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics.</li><li>The famine of 1932–1933 known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holodomor">Holodomor</a>, caused by Stalin's regime's agricultural policies, cost an estimated 2.6 million to 10 million lives; whether it was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> is disputed.</li><li>On 24 August 1991 the Supreme Soviet adopted the Act of Declaration of Independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, and on 1 December 92.3% of voters voted for independence.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Although it was part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, the Ukrainian SSR was a founding member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> in 1945 and an elected member of the Security Council in 1948–1949 and 1984–1985.</p></aside>
    </section>

